4. COMMERCIAL USE AND ROYALTY

   4.1 Scope

   This section applies to your use of the Software in any Product if
   any of the following is true:

   (a) the Product generates revenue, directly or indirectly;
   (b) the Product is used internally by a for-profit organization to
       support a revenue-generating activity.

   "Product" means any software you distribute, sell, license, make
   available as a service to third parties.

   "Product Revenue" means the gross revenue attributable to the
   Product during a calendar year, including sales, subscriptions,
   licensing, advertising, and in-app purchases.

   4.2 Royalty terms

   (a) Threshold: no royalty is due on the first USD $100,000 of
       Product Revenue in any calendar year.

   (b) Rate: a royalty of 1% (one percent) is due on all Product
       Revenue above the Threshold in that calendar year.

   (c) Cap: the total royalty due for a single Product in a single
       calendar year will not exceed USD $600,000.

   Example: a Product with USD $2,100,000 in Product Revenue in a
   calendar year owes 1% of USD $2,000,000, i.e. USD $20,000. A
   Product with USD $100,000,000 in Product Revenue owes the Cap,
   USD $600,000.

   4.3 Notification and payment

   Within 30 days of a Product first exceeding the Threshold, you
   must notify the copyright holder at gabriel.readme@hey.com,
   identifying the Product and confirming acceptance of these terms
   in writing.

   Royalties are self-reported and paid annually, within 60 days of
   the end of each calendar year, together with a statement of
   Product Revenue for that year. The copyright holder may request
   reasonable documentation supporting the statement.

   4.4 Exemptions

   This section does not apply, and the Software remains free, when:

   (i) the Product is distributed under an OSI-approved open-source
       license;
   (ii) the user is a natural person, or a group of natural persons,
        using the Product for personal or non-commercial purposes, AND
        no organization meeting criterion 4.1(b) has any ownership or
        operational interest in the Product; or
   (iii) the user is a non-profit organization using the Product in
         furtherance of its non-profit mission.

   4.5 Changes to terms

   The Threshold, Rate and Cap above apply to the version of the
   Software you adopted. The copyright holder may change them in
   future versions of this license, but such changes apply only to
   versions of the Software released under the changed license.

5. LIMITED MAINTENANCE COMMITMENT

   For users whose Product has exceeded the Threshold under §4 and
   whose royalty payments are current, the copyright holder commits to:

   (a) shipping bug fixes in regular releases of the Software; and
   (b) issuing security patches for the major version the user has
       adopted, for 18 months after that version's release.

   No other warranty, support obligation, response-time guarantee, or
   service-level commitment is granted, express or implied. This
   commitment lapses if royalty payments are more than 60 days overdue.

